0 A battery box and two receivers feed a bench-top cluster of four Power Functions motors.
0 Name: ELECTRIC_POWER_FUNCTION_CABLE-Constraints.ldr
0 Author: Holly Wood
0 Unofficial Model
0 // Scene: The tall battery box stands behind two smaller receiver units. Large rounded motors and slimmer rectangular motors spread outward, joined by straight leads, slack loops and coils.
0 // Rigid construction: 58119 is the battery box, 58123 the receiver, 58121 the XL motor and 58120 the medium motor. Separate 58124c01 plugs make the cable interfaces visible.
0 // Build lesson: Give an industrial model a readable power layout: battery access, receiver access, purposeful motor placement and restrained cable routing around the frame.
0 // Reuse: The scattered modules still need mounts, output couplings and a chassis. Cable display colours do not identify voltage, polarity or electrical channels.
0 ROTATION CENTER 0 0 0 1 "Custom" 
0 ROTATION CONFIG 0 0
